  "rationale": "Resubmission of the checker-accepted stream from rounds 1-3 with identical structure and metrics. C (80x16) is processed as five 16-row tiles, each requiring two K-chunk products (k=32 = 2x16) reduced in increasing K order: the first compute overwrites the accumulator tile, the second accumulates, then one mvout stores the finished C tile. The 32-row scratchpad holds exactly one 16-row A tile (rows 0-15) plus one 16-row B tile (rows 16-31), so B cannot stay resident across A reloads. DMA input bytes are at the proven lower bound of 4096: all 10 distinct A tiles (offset i*512 + j*16) are loaded exactly once (2560 bytes), and each B tile needs at least ceil(5/2)=3 loads because the 2-tile accumulator space permits at most two computes per B residency before accumulate+mvout must free an accumulator; the pairing schedule achieves this (6 B mvins = 1536 bytes): one B0 load serves the chunk-0 computes of two consecutive C tiles, then one B1 load serves both chunk-1 computes. Command count is at its floor: 1 config_ex + 2 config_ld (A stride 32 vs B stride 16 require both slots) + 1 config_st (store stride 64 = 16 int32 per C row) + 16 mvin + 10 preload (one per compute, mandatory) + 10 compute + 5 mvout + 1 final fence = 46. out_addr layout: bit31 (accumulator space) + bit29 (full 32-bit C width) + bit30 set only on accumulate-stage preloads, low bits 0/16 select the two accumulator tiles; every compute uses accumulated=false with the B tile staged by the immediately preceding preload and bd_spad_addr = GARBAGE_ADDR (4294967295). Accepted in rounds 1-3 with 4096 DMA input bytes and 46 commands, matching lower bounds on both objectives."
